<rss version="2.0"><channel><title>Annotations by Pablo Caro - Programación</title><link>/en/</link><description>Anotaciones</description><lastBuildDate>Sun, 03 May 2026 15:23:00 +0200</lastBuildDate><item><title>Pi subagent extensions: TintinWeb, NicoBailon and Taskplane</title><link>/en/extensiones-subagentes-pi</link><description>&lt;p&gt;A comparison of three extensions for running subagents in pi — TintinWeb, NicoBailon, and Taskplane — each with a different approach.&lt;/p&gt;</description><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Pablo Caro</dc:creator><pubDate>Sun, 03 May 2026 15:23:00 +0200</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="false">tag:None,2026-05-03:/en/extensiones-subagentes-pi</guid><category>Programación</category><category>pi</category><category>coding-agent</category><category>subagentes</category><category>extensiones</category><category>cli</category><category>herramientas</category></item><item><title>Rust eBooks Nightly — Rust books in EPUB, AZW3, MOBI, and PDF</title><link>/en/rust-ebooks-nightly</link><description>&lt;p&gt;Artur Sulej's project that automatically builds and publishes the latest versions of top Rust books as eBooks. Updated daily.&lt;/p&gt;</description><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Pablo Caro</dc:creator><pubDate>Tue, 21 Apr 2026 22:00:00 +0200</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="false">tag:None,2026-04-21:/en/rust-ebooks-nightly</guid><category>Programación</category><category>rust</category><category>ebooks</category><category>epub</category><category>calibre</category><category>github actions</category></item><item><title>Disable git autocrlf</title><link>/en/disable-git-autocrlf</link><description>&lt;p&gt;If you use Windows (or WSL), Git has been silently converting your line endings. One command fixes it.&lt;/p&gt;</description><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Pablo Caro</dc:creator><pubDate>Tue, 21 Apr 2026 12:00:00 +0200</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="false">tag:None,2026-04-21:/en/disable-git-autocrlf</guid><category>Programación</category><category>git</category><category>windows</category><category>wsl</category><category>line endings</category></item><item><title>Installing GitHub Skills</title><link>/en/installing-github-skills</link><description>&lt;p&gt;Comparing &lt;code&gt;gh skill&lt;/code&gt; vs &lt;code&gt;npx skills&lt;/code&gt; for installing and managing AI agent skills.&lt;/p&gt;</description><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Pablo Caro</dc:creator><pubDate>Sun, 19 Apr 2026 12:00:00 +0200</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="false">tag:None,2026-04-19:/en/installing-github-skills</guid><category>Programación</category><category>github</category><category>cli</category><category>agentes-ia</category><category>skills</category></item><item><title>Crit: The Review Loop for Agents</title><link>/en/crit-review-loop-agents</link><description>&lt;p&gt;Crit is a tool designed to close the code review loop for AI-generated code, providing an intuitive and efficient web interface.&lt;/p&gt;</description><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Pablo Caro</dc:creator><pubDate>Sun, 22 Mar 2026 14:49:00 +0100</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="false">tag:None,2026-03-22:/en/crit-review-loop-agents</guid><category>Programación</category><category>ia</category><category>agents</category><category>review</category><category>opencode</category><category>productividad</category></item><item><title>sem: Semantic Version Control</title><link>/en/sem-semantic-version-control</link><description>&lt;p&gt;Discovering sem, a CLI tool that understands your code's semantics and tells you what entities changed, not just what lines.&lt;/p&gt;</description><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Pablo Caro</dc:creator><pubDate>Sun, 15 Mar 2026 14:11:00 +0100</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="false">tag:None,2026-03-15:/en/sem-semantic-version-control</guid><category>Programación</category><category>cli</category><catego